        {
          "id": "derive-1-2",
          "step": "1.2",
          "claim": "If $\\mathcal H=\\{h_0\\}$, then initially $V=\\{h_0\\}$; after any query-free scan step it remains that singleton. Thus every $u_i$ is unanimous with label $h_0(u_i)=h^*(u_i)$ by [F1]. Since [F2] tests unanimity before the budget condition, the procedure predicts each index and never queries, even when $b=0$.",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "F1",
            "F2",
            "construct"
